  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "Calculate \\((x+3)(x-3)\\), and find its value when \\(x=5\\).",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "16",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\((x+3)(x-3)=x^2-9\\). When \\(x=5\\), its value is \\(25-9=16\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Expand and cancel the middle terms\n\nMultiplying each term in the first factor by each term in the second shows why the middle terms cancel:\n\\[\n(x+3)(x-3)=x^2-3x+3x-9=x^2-9.\n\\]\nWhen \\(x=5\\), the value is \\(5^2-9=16\\). Thus the simplified expression is \\(x^2-9\\), and its requested value is \\(16\\).",
